def spec_text():
    titles=["Purpose","Layer Model","Closed Enum Registry","Identifier Domains","Normative Requirement Schema","Implementation Requirement Schema","Implementation Instruction","ValidationResult","EvaluationResult","Evaluator Error","Evaluator Contract","Error Policy","Error Classification","Conformance Result","Explicit Conversion Matrix","State Transition Guard","Certificate Transitions","Release Execution Transitions","Event Contract","Projection Contract","Decision-Basis Reuse","Typed Pipeline","Rust Type-State Boundary","Conformance Test Categories","Minimum Negative Test Set","Machine-Checkable Invariants","Updated Artifact Tree","What R6 Resolves","What R6 Does Not Yet Define","Closure Assessment"]
    statements=["R6 converts frozen R5 semantics into a machine-oriented contract and introduces no semantic state.","Five planes are explicit and no plane implicitly inherits authority.","The supplied sixteen machine enums and four inherited frozen domains reject unknown values.","Semantic identifier domains remain distinct even when serialized as strings.","Normative obligations remain technology-neutral and machine-representable.","Implementation requirements require traceable normative and profile origins.","Instruction mandatory flags apply only within owning implementation authority.","Validation controls processing eligibility and never establishes proposition truth.","EvaluationResult records a completed evaluation and remains distinct from error.","Twelve observable errors preserve the eleven supplied codes plus inherited dependency-unavailable coverage.","Evaluator returns Result<EvaluationResult, EvaluationError> and has no higher-layer authority.","Error defaults to evaluation failure; semantic mapping requires explicit profile policy.","Infrastructure failure never becomes a false claim about the subject.","Conformance is requirement-bound and cannot be inferred from isolated TRUE.","Five named conversion contracts replace generic conversion.","State changes require structural, reference, integrity, temporal, scope, authority, and transition checks.","Only the five supplied certificate lifecycle edges are legal.","Only the six supplied release-execution edges are legal.","Invalid events are rejected in the declared validation order and never repaired.","Projection is deterministic from validated history, profile, and algorithm.","Changed decision basis is NOT_REUSABLE absent explicit safe compatibility.","Typed stages preserve independent validation, evaluation, conformance, authorization, decision, execution, and verification.","Typestate is an implementation technique; equivalent machine-checkable boundaries are required.","T1 through T7 are executable and mandatory.","N-001 through N-018 are executable negative vectors.","R6-I01 through R6-I18 are executable invariants.","Artifacts are physically grouped by semantics, plane, runtime, errors, conversions, transitions, Rust, and tests.","Closed enums, authority separation, and result/error separation resolve the supplied practical ambiguities.","Concrete production backends, predicate language, concurrency, and target integration remain implementation-only.","The machine contract is realized without v14.8 or a new semantic state; production implementation remains unverified."]
    return "# v14.7-R6 — Machine Schema and Typed Domain Realization\n\n"+"\n\n".join(f"## {i}. {title}\n{statements[i-1]}" for i,title in enumerate(titles,1))+"\n\n## Final Principle\nSemantic authority belongs to the defining layer. Evaluation produces a semantic result only on contractual completion; otherwise it produces an explicit evaluator error interpreted only by explicit policy.\n"

